### Admin API — Interlinear Bible
### Requires REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
###
### Service layout:
###   admin  :8081  — Flyway migrations, all pipeline endpoints
###   reader :8080  — no Flyway, no admin endpoints, production-like
###   batch  :8083  — second admin for long background runs (standalone sense disambiguation)
###                   start with:  ./dev.sh batch

@admin      = http://localhost:8081/api/admin
@batchAdmin = http://localhost:8083/api/admin
@reader     = http://localhost:8080/api

### Tune these for the chapter you are working on
#- =============================================================================
#- BOOK ID REFERENCE
#- =============================================================================
#- 40 Matthew  41 Mark     42 Luke     43 John     44 Acts
#- 45 Romans   46 1Cor     47 2Cor     48 Gal      49 Eph
#- 50 Phil      51 Col      52 1Thess  53 2Thess   54 1Tim
#- 55 2Tim      56 Titus    57 Phlm    58 Heb      59 Jas
#- 60 1Pet      61 2Pet     62 1John   63 2John    64 3John
#- 65 Jude      66 Rev
@bookId  = 43
@chapter = 1
@lang    = en
@delayMs = 1000

### Set after staging a contextual gloss chapter — copy filename from staging response
@stagingFile = contextual_gloss_B43_C1_en_REPLACE_WITH_TIMESTAMP.json

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BOOTSTRAP
# Two paths to a working DB:
#   Path 1 — full pipeline: reimport raw data → corpus → rules → lexicons → translations
#             Use for a fresh environment or after source-file changes.
#   Path 2 — JSON restore: load exported cluster-gloss-rules JSON → apply to cache
#             Standard deployment path — fast, no AI calls needed.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Pipeline status — stale flags and pending steps
GET {{admin}}/pipeline/status

###

### Prompt cache status — which prompts are loaded
GET {{admin}}/prompts/status

###

### Reload prompts from disk — edit a .txt file in src/main/resources/prompts/ then call this
###   No restart needed during ./dev.sh (spring-boot:run serves resources directly from disk)
POST {{admin}}/prompts/reload

###

### Override a prompt in-memory for testing (does NOT write to file — restart to revert)
###   Workflow: PUT new text → test via import-sense-selections → restart to revert
PUT {{admin}}/prompts/sense-batch-system
Content-Type: text/plain

You are a Greek New Testament lexical sense classifier.
Given a verse reference and a numbered list of Greek words, select the most
appropriate sense for each word from its listed options.
Return JSON array only. No explanation.

###

### Path 1 — full pipeline from raw data (first-time setup)
POST {{admin}}/bootstrap?path=1

###

### Path 2 — JSON restore (standard deploy: load rules JSON, apply to cache)
POST {{admin}}/bootstrap?path=2

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DATA IMPORT
# Run in this order for a fresh DB. Each step is idempotent (safe to re-run).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 1. Reimport word tokens from MorphGNT/OpenGNT (truncates verse_word, verse, lexeme_occurrence)
POST {{admin}}/reimport-words

###

### 2. Import AI-synthesized corpus glosses (lexeme_meaning source='corpus')
###    Triggers Handler B (gloss chain) automatically in background on completion
POST {{admin}}/import-corpus?reset=true

###

### 3. Lexicon sources — add in any order, all write to lexeme_meaning
POST {{admin}}/import-stepbible-lexicons?reset=true

###

POST {{admin}}/import-thayer?reset=true

###

POST {{admin}}/import-ugl?reset=true

###

### Strong's definitions + GK glosses (enrichments on top of existing lexeme rows)
POST {{admin}}/import-lexicon-enrichments

###

POST {{admin}}/import-etymology?reset=true

###

POST {{admin}}/import-net-meanings

###

### 4. Bible translations (BSB, KJV, NET, WEB, ASV, LEB, YLT, BBE, ULT)
POST {{admin}}/import-all-translations

###

### Single translation
POST {{admin}}/import-translation?code=BSB

###

### 5. Library books (MyBible format)
POST {{admin}}/import-library?reset=true

###

### Fix gap lemma links — repairs missing lexeme links from OpenGNT CSV
POST {{admin}}/fix-gap-lemma-links

###

### Inspect NT lexemes
GET {{admin}}/lexemes

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HANDLER A — MORPHOLOGY KEYS
# Computes normalized morph_key on every verse_word row.
# Runs automatically as part of regenerate-lite-glosses — only call directly
# to backfill after a reimport-words without running the full gloss regen.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Populate morph_key on all 138K verse_word rows
POST {{admin}}/populate-morph-keys

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HANDLER B — LITE GLOSS PIPELINE
# Generates short English glosses for every token using the rules engine.
# Normal flow: regenerate-lite-glosses (builds rules + applies them in one step).
# Path 2 restore flow: import-cluster-gloss-rules → apply-cluster-gloss-rules.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Regenerate all 138K LITE glosses from scratch (~30-60s)
###   Runs Handler A (morph keys) first, then builds cluster_gloss_rule, then writes gloss_set_entry
POST {{admin}}/regenerate-lite-glosses

###

### Populate cluster_gloss_rule only (without rewriting gloss_set_entry)
POST {{admin}}/populate-cluster-gloss-rules

###

### Path 2 restore — apply already-imported cluster_gloss_rule rows to gloss_set_entry
###   Run after: import-cluster-gloss-rules?lang=en and ?lang=es
POST {{admin}}/apply-cluster-gloss-rules

###

### Export cluster gloss rules for one language to JSON
POST {{admin}}/export-cluster-gloss-rules?lang=en

###

### Export cluster gloss rules for ALL languages
POST {{admin}}/export-cluster-gloss-rules/all

###

### Import cluster gloss rules from JSON (Path 2 restore step 1)
POST {{admin}}/import-cluster-gloss-rules?lang=en

###

### Override a single cluster_gloss_rule entry
PUT {{admin}}/cluster-gloss-rule
Content-Type: application/json

{"strongsId": "G1344", "morphKey": "verb_aorist_passive_ptcp_nom_sg_m", "gloss": "having been justified"}

# ── Irregular Verb Enrichment (feeds back into Handler B) ─────────────────────

### Preview enrichment for specific verbs (dry run — no writes)
POST {{admin}}/preview-verb-enrichment?strongsIds=G1510,G2064

###

### Enrich all irregular verbs via Groq AI (writes to irregular_verb_form)
POST {{admin}}/enrich-irregular-verbs

###

### Apply stored enrichments to gloss pipeline, triggers gloss chain cascade
POST {{admin}}/apply-irregular-verb-enrichments

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HANDLER C — SENSE DISAMBIGUATION (AI)
# Determines the correct sense for each multi-sense token in context.
# Writes to token_sense_override. After running, gloss chain must be re-run
# so LITE glosses reflect the selected sense (done automatically unless standalone).
#
# Two modes:
#
#   Default (standalone=false)
#     One transaction. Gloss chain fires automatically on completion.
#     Use for: spot-checks, single chapter/verse, CI tests.
#
#   Standalone (standalone=true)  ← run on batchAdmin :8083
#     Per-chapter transactions — crash-safe, each chapter committed independently.
#     Re-running skips chapters already in token_sense_override.
#     Gloss chain does NOT fire — call regenerate-lite-glosses manually when done.
#     Use for: full-NT overnight runs without blocking dev on :8081.
# =============================================================================
#- BOOK ID REFERENCE
#- =============================================================================

#- 40 Matthew  41 Mark     42 Luke     43 John     44 Acts
#- 45 Romans   46 1Cor     47 2Cor     48 Gal      49 Eph
#- 50 Phil      51 Col      52 1Thess  53 2Thess   54 1Tim
#- 55 2Tim      56 Titus    57 Phlm    58 Heb      59 Jas
#- 60 1Pet      61 2Pet     62 1John   63 2John    64 3John
#- 65 Jude      66 Rev
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Spot-check — one verse (returns selections list for inspection)
POST {{admin}}/import-sense-selections?bookId={{bookId}}&chapter={{chapter}}&verse=1

###

### Single chapter (returns selections list — useful for verifying specific passages)
POST {{admin}}/import-sense-selections?bookId={{bookId}}&chapter={{chapter}}

###

### Full NT — single transaction, triggers gloss chain on completion
###   Only use if you can keep admin running for the full 3-6 hour run.
###   A crash loses all progress.
POST {{admin}}/import-sense-selections

###

### ── Standalone mode — use batchAdmin (:8083) ──────────────────────────────
###   Start batch admin first:  ./dev.sh batch
###   Each chapter commits independently. Safe to kill and resume.

### Full NT standalone run (all chapters, no cascade)
POST {{batchAdmin}}/import-sense-selections?standalone=true

###

### Single book standalone
POST {{batchAdmin}}/import-sense-selections?standalone=true&bookId={{bookId}}

###

### After standalone run completes — trigger gloss chain manually
POST {{batchAdmin}}/regenerate-lite-glosses

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LANGUAGE GLOSSES (non-English, Groq AI)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Generate non-English LITE glosses
POST {{admin}}/generate-language-glosses?lang=es&delayMs=2000

###

### Check generation progress
GET {{admin}}/language-gloss-status?lang=es

###

### Expand generated glosses into gloss_set_entry cache
POST {{admin}}/expand-language-gloss-set?lang=es

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CONTEXTUAL GLOSS (#118, #122)
# Staged workflow — AI writes to ai_staging/ file first, reviewed, then committed.
# No DB writes until you explicitly call /commit.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Status — how many verses are committed to contextual_gloss
GET {{admin}}/contextual-gloss/status?lang={{lang}}

###

### Stage one chapter (writes ai_staging/ file, does NOT touch DB)
POST {{admin}}/populate-contextual-glosses/chapter?bookId={{bookId}}&chapter={{chapter}}&lang={{lang}}&reset=false&delayMs={{delayMs}}

###

### Stage one chapter — force re-generate even if staging file already exists
POST {{admin}}/populate-contextual-glosses/chapter?bookId={{bookId}}&chapter={{chapter}}&lang={{lang}}&reset=true&delayMs={{delayMs}}

###

### List staging files for a specific chapter
GET {{admin}}/contextual-gloss/staging?bookId={{bookId}}&chapter={{chapter}}&lang={{lang}}

###

### List ALL staging files
GET {{admin}}/contextual-gloss/staging

###

### Commit staging file — writes to contextual_gloss, marks file committed
POST {{admin}}/contextual-gloss/staging/{{stagingFile}}/commit

###

### Stage entire NT in background (one file per chapter — run overnight)
POST {{admin}}/populate-contextual-glosses/all?lang={{lang}}&reset=false&delayMs={{delayMs}}

###

### Purge contextual_gloss for non-polysemous lexemes (one chapter)
POST {{admin}}/contextual-gloss/purge-non-polysemous?bookId={{bookId}}&chapter={{chapter}}&lang={{lang}}

###

### Purge ALL non-polysemous contextual glosses (entire NT)
POST {{admin}}/contextual-gloss/purge-non-polysemous?lang=en

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AI TRANSLATION STRIP (#119)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Status — how many verses have AI translations
GET {{admin}}/ai-translation/status?lang={{lang}}

###

### Populate single chapter
POST {{admin}}/populate-ai-translations/chapter?bookId={{bookId}}&chapter={{chapter}}&lang={{lang}}&reset=false&delayMs={{delayMs}}

###

### Populate single chapter — reset existing
POST {{admin}}/populate-ai-translations/chapter?bookId={{bookId}}&chapter={{chapter}}&lang={{lang}}&reset=true&delayMs={{delayMs}}

###

### Populate entire NT in background (run overnight)
POST {{admin}}/populate-ai-translations/all?lang={{lang}}&reset=false&delayMs={{delayMs}}

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WORD INSIGHTS (Groq AI — PRO feature)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Status — how many lemmas have pre-generated insights
GET {{admin}}/word-insights/status?minFrequency=10

###

### Populate a small batch (test before running overnight)
POST {{admin}}/populate-word-insights?minFrequency=10&limit=50&delayMs=2000

###

### Run all word insights in background (overnight)
POST {{admin}}/word-insights/run-all?minFrequency=10&delayMs=4000

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# READER — VERIFICATION
# Spot-check that reader endpoints return correct data after pipeline runs.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Available translations
GET {{reader}}/bible-translation/available

###

### Books list
GET {{reader}}/books

###

### Passage — John 1 (sense disambiguation verification)
GET {{reader}}/passage/43/1?lang={{lang}}

###

### Passage — using current bookId/chapter variables
GET {{reader}}/passage/{{bookId}}/{{chapter}}?lang={{lang}}
